:: Introduction {"position":"700,500","size":"100,100"}
Welcome to the Metadata Magnet input file setup wizard.
Completion of this form will generate a block of text which you can save as a params file (YAML format) for your pipeline run in Nextflow. (nextflow run option: -params-file my_params_file.yaml)
The inputs you enter here will be used by the pipeline to produce a FASTA that represents homologs of your protein of interest (with various kinds of optional filtering) as well as a metadata file.
The FASTA and metadata outputs may then be used as inputs to the GUI for statistical tests and visualization.



<<set $outputString to "">>
[[NEXT|blast]]


:: align {"position":"1125,2125","size":"100,100"}
Would you like to align your FASTAs automatically using this pipeline?
MUSCLE/super5 is selected based on the size of the final FASTA.
If you require greater control over the alignment method, please select 'no' and find the FASTAs in the fasta/not_aligned subdirectory of the output directory. 


[[YES|align2]]
[[NO|finalizeOutputs]]



:: align2 {"position":"1250,2250","size":"100,100"}
<<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "align", "true") >>
<<goto "finalizeOutputs">>


:: blast {"position":"700,625","size":"100,100"}
Collecting inputs for BLAST.
Please enter the path to the FASTA containing your query sequence. Ensure that the FASTA contains only one sequence.


<input id="queryInput" type="text">
<<button "Submit path to query FASTA">>
    <<set $queryFasta = $("#queryInput").val()>>
    <<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "queryFasta", $queryFasta) >>
    <<goto "blast2">>
<</button>>


:: blast2 {"position":"700,750","size":"100,100"}
Please enter the path to the directory containing the BLAST db files.


<input id="blastPathInput" type="text">
<<button "Submit blast db path">>
    <<set $blastPath = $("#blastPathInput").val()>>
    <<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "blastPath", $blastPath) >>
    <<goto "blast3">>
<</button>>





:: blast3 {"position":"700,875","size":"100,100"}
Please enter the name/title of your BLAST database. This is the part of the filename that is shared across the BLAST db files, not including extensions. 


<input id="blastNameInput" type="text">
<<button "Submit blast db name">>
    <<set $blastName = $("#blastNameInput").val()>>
    <<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "blastName", $blastName) >>
    <<goto "blast4">>
<</button>>




:: blast4 {"position":"700,1000","size":"100,100"}
In the BLAST file, do you anticipate protein IDs to be in the format genomeID-proteinID?
This would be the case if you use the provided script to make a blast DB from a genome DB.


[[YES|separateIDsYes]]
[[NO|separateIDsNo]]



:: endEarly {"position":"850,1375","size":"100,100"}
You will see the parameters file on the next screen.
First run the pipeline with this inputs YAML file, and inspect the output BLAST file. 
When you are ready to continue, rerun this wizard with the exact same set of arguments as defined previously, and then rerun the pipeline with the new inputs YAML file and the -resume flag to use cached outputs.


[[FINISH|printOutputs]]


:: evalueYes {"position":"500,1500","size":"100,100"}
Please enter an evalue threshold. Sequences with evalue <= this threshold will be kept.
For scientific notation, please use e or E, e.g. 1e-30.


<input id="evalueInput" type="text">
<<button "Submit evalue threshold">>
    <<set $evalueThreshold = $("#evalueInput").val()>>
    <<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "evalueThreshold", $evalueThreshold) >>
    <<goto "filter2">>
<</button>>


:: filter1 {"position":"625,1375","size":"100,100"}
Would you like to filter by evalue?


[[YES|evalueYes]]
[[NO|filter2]]


:: filter2 {"position":"625,1625","size":"100,100"}
Would you like to filter to the top hit (sequence with lowest evalue, keeping only one in the event of a tie) per ORGANISM?
Different strains of the same bacteria are considered separate organisms.

[[YES|organismYes]]
[[NO|filter3]]






:: filter3 {"position":"750,1750","size":"100,100"}
<<set $filterByGenome to false>> /%initialize%/

Would you like to filter to the top hit (sequence with lowest evalue, keeping only one in the event of a tie) per GENOME?


[[YES|genomeYes]]
[[NO|filter4]]




:: filter4 {"position":"875,1875","size":"100,100"}
<<set $filterBySynteny to false>> /%initialize%/

Would you like to filter by synteny context?


[[YES|synteny1]]
[[NO|retrieveMetadata]]




:: filterNow {"position":"750,1250","size":"100,100"}
You may specify in advance the filtering thresholds for the BLAST hits for your query sequence according to certain criteria.
But would you like to inspect the BLAST hits manually before filtering?


[[YES|endEarly]]
[[NO|filter1]]


:: finalizeOutputs {"position":"725,1500","size":"100,100"}
Paste the text on the next screen into a text file.
If your text file is named inputs.yaml, then you can use it by running: nextflow run main.nf -params-file inputs.yaml

[[NEXT|printOutputs]]




:: genomeYes {"position":"750,1875","size":"100,100"}
