:: synteny1 {"position":"875,2000","size":"100,100"}
<<set $filterBySynteny to true>>

Please prepare inputs after referring to Pynteny documentation and this pipeline's provided example synteny search inputs.
           
Please enter the path to the genome database directory in which to perform the synteny searches. 
This is a directory in which all subdirectories are named after assembly accessions, and each subdirectory contains a .gbff.gz file (unzipped is fine too).


<input id="genomeDBsyntenyInput" type="text">
<<button "Submit genome database">>
    <<set $genomeDBsynteny = $("#genomeDBsyntenyInput").val()>>
    <<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "genomeDBsynteny", $genomeDBsynteny) >>
    <<goto "synteny2">>
<</button>>





:: synteny2 {"position":"875,2125","size":"100,100"}
