:: synteny6 {"position":"875,2625","size":"100,100"}
After the synteny context search is performed, the outputs of that search will be intersected with the set of sequences from the BLAST (with any filtering specified earlier),
and the intersection will return the subset of sequences from the synteny context search that closely resemble sequences among the BLAST hits.
More specifically, the synteny hits will be blasted against a database made from the BLAST hits.

You may now specify filtering thresholds for pident (percent identity) and qcovs (query coverage per subject) for this intersection blast.
Based on these thresholds, a subset of the hits from the synteny search (i.e. homologs that appear in the specified synteny context) will be kept.
Refer to BLAST documentation: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK279684/#appendices.Options_for_the_commandline_a

[[NEXT|synteny7]]




:: synteny7 {"position":"875,2750","size":"100,100"}
Would you like to specify a pident threshold different from the default of 99?

[[YES|pidentYes]]
[[NO|synteny8]]
            





:: synteny8 {"position":"1000,2875","size":"100,100"}
Would you like to specify a qcovs threshold different from the default of 90?


[[YES|synteny9]]
[[NO|retrieveMetadata]]




:: synteny9 {"position":"1000,3000","size":"100,100"}
Please specify a qcovs threshold as a number from 0 to 100. 
The filtering will keep only synteny hit sequences with qcovs >= this threshold in the intersection BLAST. 


<input id="intersectQcovsInput" type="text">
<<button "Submit qcovs threshold">>
    <<set $intersectQcovs = $("#intersectQcovsInput").val()>>
    <<set $outputString to setup.formatInput($outputString, "intersectQcovs", $intersectQcovs) >>
    <<goto "retrieveMetadata">>
<</button>>



:: StoryScript [script]
setup.trimInput = function(input) {
  // remove surrounding whitespace
  let trimmed = input.trim();

  // remove surrounding quotes if present
  if (
    (trimmed.startsWith('"') && trimmed.endsWith('"')) ||
    (trimmed.startsWith("'") && trimmed.endsWith("'")) ||
    (trimmed.startsWith('`') && trimmed.endsWith('`'))
  ) {
    trimmed = trimmed.slice(1, -1);
  }

  return trimmed;
}


setup.formatInput = function(currentOutput, varName, input) {
  let outputString = currentOutput + varName + ": " + setup.trimInput(input) + "\n";
  return outputString
}
